

1. Object-oriented programming uses classes and objects. What are classes and what are objects? What is the relationship between classes and objects?

### Class

A **class** is a blueprint or template used to create objects. It defines the properties (variables) and behaviors (methods) of objects.

### Object

An **object** is an instance of a class. It occupies memory and can access the members of the class.

### Relationship

* A class defines the structure.
* Objects are created from the class.
* One class can have many objects.

### Example

```java
class Student {
    String name;
    int age;

    void display() {
        System.out.println(name + " " + age);
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String args[]) {
        Student s1 = new Student();
        s1.name = "Rahul";
        s1.age = 20;
        s1.display();
    }
}
```

