# 10. When do we declare the members of the class as static? Explain with example.

Use **static** when a member belongs to the class instead of individual objects.

Example

```java
class Student {
    static String college = "GCETTS";
    String name;
}
```

All objects share the same college.

Access:

```java
System.out.println(Student.college);
```

