# 13. Explain about inner classes with an example.

An **inner class** is a class declared inside another class.

Example

```java
class Outer {

    class Inner {
        void display() {
            System.out.println("Inner Class");
        }
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String args[]) {
        Outer obj = new Outer();
        Outer.Inner in = obj.new Inner();
        in.display();
    }
}
```

Advantages:

* Better encapsulation
* Logical grouping
* Access outer class members

