# 16. When does a base class variable get hidden? Give reasons.

A base class variable is hidden when the subclass declares another variable with the **same name**.

Example

```java
class A {
    int x = 10;
}

class B extends A {
    int x = 20;
}
```

Reason:
The subclass variable hides the superclass variable because Java uses **variable hiding**, not variable overriding, for fields.

---

# 17. Explain with an example how we can access a hidden base class variable.

Use the **super** keyword.

Example

```java
class A {
    int x = 10;
}

class B extends A {

    int x = 20;

    void display() {
        System.out.println(super.x);
        System.out.println(x);
    }
}
```

Output

```
10
20
```

